{"id": "EUVD-2026-103649", "enisaUuid": "fc81ecfc-5c70-3dad-a766-2488a61ed321", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novpn: replace bind when learning local endpoint\n\nstruct ovpn_bind is published through peer->bind with RCU, but local\nendpoint learning updates bind->local in place under peer->lock. UDP TX\nreads the field without that lock. In particular, a concurrent IPv6\nupdate can therefore result in a torn address read.\n\nUse ovpn_peer_reset_sockaddr to publish a replacement bind when learning\na new local endpoint, just as a remote endpoint change does. Preserve\nthe current remote address and reset the dst cache only after the new\nbind has been published successfully.\n\nTrack remote endpoint changes separately so that float notification and\ntransport-address rehashing remain limited to actual peer floats.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21dbc9f4d0bdd3b22f91beabc7840064bf11594f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e283009151d3d131447c2edda500199c5fda5f72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aea934a221ec6a867221e5b765f65f1857befd53"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hmmp-5rq5-qfff", "CVE-2026-98604"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "23653063-c5e3-3635-a1e5-0d2814b62b7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "55a0c927-6fb7-3d9a-84ab-b9ad36a48f7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "6844566b-774b-3583-bb8f-8de27e95844f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "6bee84cf-1c7b-38fd-887c-91f8ea138bca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "94436d12-1082-388f-b8b2-bda04085715c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0281c1d3732d1ec084fa1e06d1767d33e1a570e <aea934a221ec6a867221e5b765f65f1857befd53"}, {"id": "a39dd1c8-6382-3f40-b5ef-2f9b507ec5d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0281c1d3732d1ec084fa1e06d1767d33e1a570e <e283009151d3d131447c2edda500199c5fda5f72"}, {"id": "c8775566-47df-3d03-ba7c-99ba7cb7daaa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "f03c501c-d3fd-3e78-b3ef-33b0c2e965b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f0281c1d3732d1ec084fa1e06d1767d33e1a570e <21dbc9f4d0bdd3b22f91beabc7840064bf11594f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e1afa0da-ccc5-3fcd-9c10-e5ba960ccbc6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}